From 492162703cbd734bba4275ea318fa5474d17d914 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:06:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): file the upstream-conflict owner card in a fresh
 interpreter [daveey]

hermes update imports hermes_cli.config_effective at startup, then moves the
checkout. report() imported the kanban modules from the new files in that same
process, so the new kanban_capabilities asked the stale config_effective for
load_profile_config_effective and validate_assignment refused the card as a
capability mismatch (mini, 2026-11-01 09:29 PT; defect kanban-c50ee42be6).

report() now runs the filing in a runtime_command child pinned to the same
HERMES_HOME and returns the id from a marker line; failures warn and log the
child's stderr tail. A conflict with no owner now prints a fixed
'Repair owner: NOT FILED' line for the signal detector.

Test: stale config_effective stub in sys.modules; report() must still file one
card and refresh it on the next call (red before, green after).
---
 hermes_cli/update_cmd_git.py                  |  4 +-
 hermes_cli/update_upstream_conflict.py        | 56 ++++++++++++---
 .../test_update_upstream_conflict.py          | 71 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_update_upstream_conflict.py

